          "lastModified": "2026-10-22T15:09:46.155Z"
        }
      }
    },
    "optimizedContext": {
      "value": "# Kernel\n\n## Rules\n- `Kernel` mounts concrete use cases under `changes`, `specs`, `project`; public application use cases require entry and wiring, except `_shared/` and ConfigWriter operations.\n- `createKernel(config, options?)` returns immutable plain object through shared `CompositionResolver`: repositories, lazy `SchemaProvider`, hooks, hashing, parsers, registries.\n- Use cases receive `SchemaProvider`, never direct `SchemaRegistry.resolve()`. Schema failures not cached; hooks derive resolved schema/overrides.\n- Composition owns VCS/actor resolution and additive registries. Kernel exposes merged registry views plus `changes.repo` and `specs.repos`.\n- `FsChangeRepository.get()` detects artifact drift after `designing` or active approval, persists `artifact-drift`, accepts legacy `artifact-change`.\n- Config mutation uses `createConfigWriter()`; runtime execute inputs never re-pass creation config.\n\n## Constraints\n- Mandatory public domain facade; no business logic.\n- Config mutation and graph store outside Kernel.\n- `Kernel` and `createKernel` public; no `createKernelInternals` export.",
      "schema": {
        "name": "schema-std",
        "version": 1
      },
      "artifactState": {
        "spec.md": {
          "hash": "sha256:408a307be675fbe45019fc749f0f8300e481b8e0dabeb151f9d7c510ab2b4b60",
